{"id":"capture-files","parent":"mld950xq","ord":"a0","title":"PR: /capture takes files — photos and PDFs land in the vault","todo":true,"desc":"The file half of quick capture, split out so v1 ships text-only.\n\n**Pre-ruled 2026-08-21:** reuse the chat attachment policy — the same closed extension allowlist and 50 MB cap (`surface/src/attach.ts`) — rather than a second list. Files land in a dated vault folder (e.g. `media/captures/2026-08/`) with the capturing node linking them.\n\n**What it needs that v1 doesn't:** a binary write-into-vault path — today only chat attachments (tmp dir) and `.md` documents have write doors. That path is this PR's real work; the endpoint change is just multipart.","after":["quick-capture-door"],"see":["quick-capture-door"],"created":"2026-08-21T16:55:42-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21, ruled at quick-capture-door's brainstorm"}}
