{"id":"surface-cli-wrong-vault","parent":"e8qrp2eg","ord":"a0","title":"PR #354: every answer names the vault it wrote to (root path + server URL)","done":"2026-08-23T16:43:50-04:00","desc":"Change on #354: add `root` and `url` to every answer the CLI prints, so a write can never land somewhere unnoticed. (The wrong-vault bug itself — one socket per user, first server wins — disappears with the socket; this is the remaining part.)\n\nWhat happened 2026-08-23: the human's capture landed in this repo's docs vault because two servers shared one socket path; the answer said `file: _olai/Inbox.olai` with no root.\n\n**pr** — 6a863f38) — no socket, --url required, root+url on every answer","created":"2026-08-23T12:11:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T16:43:50-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-23 12:08: ran the README capture, the row is not in their Inbox.olai; RCA by the orchestrator","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/354","where":"packages/server/src/dial.ts:130 (rung 4 = getRuntimeSocketPath({app:'olai'}) — one path per USER); serve.ts:274-297 (a serve whose bind fails is 'narrated and carries on'); main.ts:73 socketFor"}}
