{"id":"supervision-watcher","parent":"h6d3fkzo","ord":"a1","title":"Supervision: the watcher and the mute list","desc":"**Everything goes through kolu** (graduated from instructions.md, 2026-08-25): never run, resume, or message an agent outside its kolu terminal — no headless `claude -p`, no `--resume` in a background shell, no side channels; a terminal that can't receive the instruction is a stop-and-ask. Kolu MCP is for ACTIONS only (spawn, read screens, send input, kill), always as instant calls; blocking MCP waits are banned from the supervision path.\n\n**The wake mechanism** (the one law): `kolu watch --states waiting,awaiting --held-for 60s --nag 10m --ignore <mute-list> --heartbeat 30m` run under the harness's Monitor tool with `persistent: true` (a background Bash task notifies only on exit — a watch stream never exits; RCA 2026-08-21). Fleet-wide, never an id list. It dies LOUDLY on server/process restarts: re-arm it, update the `watch-task` prop, record the re-arm here. The orchestrator babysits every spawned terminal until its PR merges — on every wake: land the event on the board before working it, then work it to a flipped mark plus a dispatched next step (or an explicit block). No turn ends with an unread event or an unsupervised live lane. `watch-task` = the live Monitor task id; `mute-list` = the ignored terminal ids, bare.\n\n**The mute list's dispositions** (ruled 2026-08-23 ~17:15; 🔥 corrected 2026-08-24; ids rotate on kaval restart — re-identify by intent/cwd, never assume):\n- `d7543299` — THE ORCHESTRATOR ITSELF: this olai ACP chat session, whose headless claude-code the padi sees as a terminal (the --ignore-self case, hand-spelled because the orchestrator runs behind the chat panel).\n- `30f81ddc` 🔥 — the human's Fable agent on kolu, engageable on their word only.\n- `724a754e` — the human's nixos-config grok (+ its splits).\n- `8bb96ee1` — the human's kolu·vide session.\n- `52e990d4` — the human's ux-review-pi spawn inside an olai worktree (theirs until handed over).\n- The GENERALIZED RULE: any terminal no lane's `terminal` prop names, outside olai's worktrees, is presumed the human's; one INSIDE olai's worktrees that the orchestrator did not create is the human's spawn until handed over. Mute only after the disposition is verified via kolu ls — never on assumption. Fail-open: a stale id costs nothing, every new terminal still rings.\n\n**Nag discipline** (RCA-2, 2026-08-21): a nag on an unchanged block is re-DERIVED, not re-acknowledged — a second nag with no new information means the block is suspect: act on standing authority or escalate as a standalone question. A dismissal applies to an event, never to a terminal.\n\nStanding rulings and dated history live in the children below (CI venue, kolu PR process, the 2026-08-21 deploy/verification).","created":"2026-08-21T17:30:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:24:12-04:00","custom":{"mute-list":"d7543299, 30f81ddc, 724a754e, 8bb96ee1, 52e990d4","watch-task":"bruxvdmue"}}
{"id":"sw-ci-venue","parent":"supervision-watcher","ord":"a0","title":"CI venue — the standing ruling","desc":"RULED by the human 2026-08-24 ~15:56 (supersedes the 2026-08-22 localhost-only ruling): kolu-ci-* boxes are back AND CAN BE USED — CI may dial them via odu's ordinary --platform path. Localhost (under `/tmp/olai-odu-localhost.lock`) and ci@petit for darwin (under `/tmp/olai-odu-petit.lock`) remain available; the once-mandatory `--host x86_64-linux=localhost` pin is lifted. For olai PRs EITHER platform green is the bar; kolu PRs need both. Admin merges are fine for a macOS-only-green olai PR (`gh pr merge --squash --admin`) — the GitHub ruleset still requires the nine x86_64-linux contexts and is deliberately not narrowed.\n\nHistory: the kolu-ci fleet was ABANDONED 2026-08-22 10:41 (Incus instability — boxes vanishing mid-e2e within ~30min of creation; the full failure transcript is https://gist.github.com/srid/143288f346ba71e27cfb54e67173e3b0), which forced the localhost/petit two-venue era, then un-abandoned 2026-08-24.","created":"2026-08-25T16:20:44-04:00"}
{"id":"sw-kolu-pr-process","parent":"supervision-watcher","ord":"a1","title":"kolu PRs ride kolu's own process","desc":"RULED by the human 2026-08-22 16:15: kolu PRs are taken through KOLU's process — the author runs kolu's /be skill (.agents/skills/be/SKILL.md in the kolu checkout) instead of our review/refactor round, and CI through kolu's /ci skill (.agents/skills/ci/SKILL.md) instead of our odu recipe; both platforms green before merge; the orchestrator merges on /be done + /ci green. 16:20: the darwin host /ci names was replaced by ci@petit (--host aarch64-darwin=ci@petit, under /tmp/olai-odu-petit.lock). Olai PRs keep our process. First applied to lane-scli PR 1 (surface-cli-kolu).","created":"2026-08-25T16:20:49-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T20:39:13-04:00"}
{"id":"sw-2026-08-21-deploy","parent":"supervision-watcher","ord":"a2","title":"2026-08-21: production deploy, double watcher death, full end-to-end verification","date":"2026-08-21","desc":"DEPLOYED ~21:20; the orchestrator's own process restarted ~21:25 — the watch died loudly both times as designed and was re-armed (bhb2ugljn). The second restart recycled every terminal id (the kolu skill's warning made real): the A/B experiment terminal died, every lane's terminal prop went stale, the mute list was rewritten.\n\nThen kolu#2194's FULL TEST with a real agent (terminal c01109d6, 21:28–21:35) — ALL STAGES PASSED: spawn+boot; typed prompt + Enter; READY in 1s; settle → test watch (--held-for 10s) transition arriving instantly (per-line flush verified); nag re-rings at exactly +45s/+90s; main watch (--held-for 60s) transition at +60s; second prompt → second transition; screen_text, kolu ls, --ignore mute list, --ignore-self, --heartbeat; loud death + re-arm twice; kill → terminal gone, state-knob watch silent by design. Verdict: GOOD — every claim exercised live on the production build.","created":"2026-08-25T16:21:00-04:00"}
{"id":"pg7obs3e","parent":"mld950xq","ord":"a2","title":"A node cannot move between outlines — the ops can't express a cross-file move","todo":true,"desc":"`move_node` deliberately never crosses files (\"trash_node is what does\") — but trash-then-recreate loses the ids: ids are unique across the set INCLUDING Trash, so the recreated nodes get new ids and every inbound reference (see, after, prop refs, mirrors, prop:key lookups by id) silently detaches. The workaround used today: recreate with new ids, trash the old subtree, fix referrers by hand — exactly the multi-step, reference-breaking dance a single op should own. Shape: either `move_node` gains a `file` target (placement moves, id keeps, references keep resolving — the same promise trash already makes about ids moving with nodes), or a dedicated `move_outline` op. The ops-only law names this pattern: an inexpressible ledger fact is a bug to file, and this is it filed.","created":"2026-08-25T16:37:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"the supervision.olai extraction, 2026-08-25 — moving one subtree out of agents.olai took recreate-under-NEW-ids + trash, because move_node is same-file by design and the duplicate-id fence counts Trash, so same-id recreation is refused"}}
{"id":"orchestrator-in-chat","parent":"j9azop3o","ord":"a1","title":"Run the orchestrator from the chat panel #human","doing":true,"desc":"- Direction (ratified 2026-08-15): orchestration lives in olai itself, driven from the chat instead of a separate terminal.\n- Three parts: agents.olai (who), a workflow template (how), lanes (what's live). See docs/brainstorming/orchestrator.md.\n- Already working: spawning worktree terminals via kolu's MCP; editing the roadmap from chat.\n- Remaining (children): author the workflow template, clone it per lane, and let olai itself watch terminals and flip marks.","changed":"2026-08-25T15:39:29-04:00","custom":{"consolidated-from":"orchestrator-home (infra → Process & orchestration, trashed on the human's word 2026-08-24 ~16:40 — one orchestrator node, this one): what it carried that survives — the rescoped ruling (the human 2026-08-21, after RCA-1 deaf-watcher and RCA-2 manufactured-gate in one afternoon) and the direction now stated by brainstorming/orchestrator.md REV 2: olai is the harness ON TOP of kolu, never launches agents, every model runs in a kolu terminal (the judge as headless claude -p on the subscription); its first-round title premise (olai drives the agent over ACP) was REJECTED by rev 2","remaining-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: two of the three Remaining children EXIST on master (dag.olai the template; lanes.olai the per-lane copies — both closed today) — the live remainder is olai-subscribes alone; and the direction line now reads through brainstorming/orchestrator.md REV 2 (olai works on top of kolu and never launches agents itself), which names this node as the home for its children when the design settles"}}
{"id":"oic-worktree","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a0","title":"MCP `lifecycle_create` cannot cut a worktree #upstream","done":"2026-08-13T21:53:22-04:00","desc":"A missing option on an existing kolu MCP verb — completing the socket so one tool call replaces spawning a terminal to type `kolu create --worktree` (debate item 9, \"fix not vault\").\n- **Shipped as kolu #2167** (merged 2026-08-14, head d983f5d0): `lifecycle_create` takes repo/worktree/run; the worktree→create→sendInput composition carries a typed partial-failure payload (stopped-partway survivor reports pinned by wire tests that fail against the pre-fix pass-through)\n- a bare create still behaves exactly as before (pinned)\n- The author named the honest residue in the PR rather than burying it: this composition now exists in four disagreeing copies across kolu's faces, and the real fix is a padi-side lifecycle.createInWorktree — architecture, deliberately out of a fixes batch\n- Directly enables olai-chat orchestration (see orchestrator-home)","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"oic-doc","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a3","title":"The charter stays at the gist — the repo copy was made and unmade","done":"2026-08-15T11:24:38-04:00","desc":"Was \"the orchestrator doc lives at a URL\".\n- **RESOLVED 2026-08-15 the opposite way it briefly went:** a repo copy at docs/orchestrator.md was made and then DELETED on the human's word — the gist (gist.github.com/srid/af6b4bcccf649fb923e4e207a7b93c51) IS the canonical charter, hand-maintained, never mirrored\n- The chat-agent-can't-read-it concern this node was filed for dissolves differently: the chat has web reach questions of its own, and the charter's future in-olai home is the workflows outline (the DAG), not a prose copy","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"agents-outline","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a4","title":"The agents outline: who, as nodes — the launch command lives in a note","done":"2026-08-15T11:20:54-04:00","desc":"Step 1 toward orchestration-in-olai (docs/brainstorming/orchestrator.md).\n\n- One node per agent, the exact launch command in its note.\n- Every launcher reads the node before spawning; a missing node refuses loudly — no machine default can decide the model again (the Fable burn's fix).\n- Zero new olai code.\n- Kolu's structured launch spec remains the later upgrade the notes would migrate into.\n- **DONE** 2026-08-15: docs/agents.olai.\n  - Born agents.jsonl — the create_outline call was handed a repo-shaped path and minted docs/docs, fixed by git mv; then PR #177's fence renamed the extension in flight.\n  - Three agents recorded: claude-opus (author), grok (reviewer, --always-approve), opencode (reviewer).\n  - Grok earned an authoring entry the same day (PR #180, solo, review waived).","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"workflow-template","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a5","title":"Write the shared workflow outline: the step DAG every lane copies","done":"2026-08-24T16:07:46-04:00","desc":"- The PR pipeline (implement → refactor → two reviews → address → CI → evidence → merge) becomes a template subtree: each step a todo node, dependencies as after-edges. The app then shows blocked-vs-ready for free.\n- Lives in ONE shared orchestration outline all repos' lanes clone from.\n- Uses only existing features: marks, after edges, notes.\n- Worked example: docs/brainstorming/orchestrator.md.","after":["node-properties"],"changed":"2026-08-24T16:07:48-04:00","custom":{"resolved":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: the artefact exists — docs/orchestrator/dag.olai (\"Workflow TEMPLATES — the pipeline a lane walks, defined ONCE as a subtree\", 11 steps with after-edges), named by instructions.md as the source"}}
{"id":"lane-cloning","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a6","title":"Dispatching a task copies the workflow DAG into its lane","done":"2026-08-24T16:07:48-04:00","desc":"- On dispatch, copy the template steps under the lane's node (real copies — each lane's steps carry their own marks).\n- Progress is marks flipping todo → doing → done, with terminal id, PR and evidence links as step properties.\n- The orchestrator's memory becomes the outline itself, and survives anything.\n- Ordering rule (from a live incident): a step that changes the worktree comes after every step that reads it. `set_doing` refusing on a blocked node (already shipped) enforces it.","after":["agents-outline","workflow-template"],"changed":"2026-08-24T16:07:51-04:00","custom":{"resolved":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: practised reality — lanes.olai carries per-lane copies with their own marks and terminal/pr/verdict/merged step properties, exercised through #365/#366 this weekend. (Superseded further the same day: the human ruled lanes MIRROR the roadmap node with dag steps inserted under the original — see lanes.olai's root desc)"}}
{"id":"node-properties","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a5V","title":"Org-style properties: facts stop living in desc strings #needs-brainstorm","done":"2026-08-15T17:46:15-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15, the human's observation on the ledger's own habit: every \"**Now** (terminal, stage, PR)\" block is structured data smuggled into desc prose — unqueryable, eyeball-parsed — and lane-cloning is about to make it systemic.\n\n- **RULED** 2026-08-15, in four rounds:\n  - Freeform key→value; brainstorm before code; full web parity in the same PR (quiet drawer under the note, ••• menu edits).\n  - Marks are not special — todo/done/date/see/after are LEGACY PROPERTIES; the record unifies into one props map, olai AUTO-MIGRATING each file's shape at startup.\n    - BUILT-IN KEYS ARE POLICED: set_prop refuses every system key toward its own verb (status→set_done and kin, date→set_date, after→set_after); set_prop owns only the keys olai does not read or write.\n    - A user key is promoted by gaining a READING, never by changing shape.\n  - The stage is NEVER a property: a lane's stage is its cloned DAG's `doing` step.\n  - Workflowy's pair joins as stamps: `created` (at capture) and `changed` (re-stamped by every write op) — no verb at all, nothing else may write them.\n    - Absent on migrated nodes (the ledger does not invent a past); appearing as nodes are touched.\n- **BRAINSTORM:** [docs/brainstorming/properties.md](/doc/docs/brainstorming/properties.md) (example-first; UNCOMMITTED, awaiting the human's review), with the interactive drawer prototype linked inside: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/48a09a59-5079-44fe-b99a-7f3a5fe49c90 (insertion order, not alphabetical — a position on open question 1).\n- **STILL OPEN:** whether search HITS carry props (one query = the lane board); whether the roadmap's existing Now blocks migrate in a sweep or rot away as lanes close.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"props-floor","parent":"node-properties","ord":"a0","title":"PR: properties, whole — the props map + migration, set_prop + search + drawer, created/changed stamps","done":"2026-08-15T17:46:07-04:00","desc":"RULED 2026-08-15 through three shapes, final.\n\n- Record unchanged + ONE open top-level key `custom` (string → text-or-list), no migration, top level closed and typo-refusing.\n- set_prop writes only custom.\n- Search: prop:key / prop:key=value.\n- Drawer with read-only system rows (id visible; zoomed always, tree rows once props exist — the human kept that at merge).\n- created/changed stamped flat, excluded from changesOf.\n- **MERGED** 2026-08-15 (the human's manual approval, the day's one reserved read): PR #179, admin-squashed at head 8d0f512e after the conflict merge with #188/#189/#190.\n  - Nix build was the sole gate at that head, a ONE-TIME exception on the human's explicit word (full odu CI stands for everything else).\n- **Journey's receipts:**\n  - Grok's same()-ignores-custom blocking fixed as a no-op guard (a same-value set_prop is a no-op everywhere).\n  - The ⌘Z double-removal on list values caught and fixed.\n  - The fresh double round found nothing further.\n- **Rulings at the gate:** drawer stays only-when-props on tree rows; hits-carry-custom filed as its own PR node.\n- **Evidence:** 1711 unit / 612 e2e / CI green at the reviewed head 5b1933e.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"doing-refuses-blocked","parent":"lane-cloning","ord":"a0","title":"PR: set_doing refuses on a blocked node — the DAG's law becomes a mechanism","done":"2026-08-15T14:22:10-04:00","desc":"Born from the 2026-08-15 incident (a rebase instructed while two reviewers still read the worktree).\n\n- set_doing on a node whose after-targets are unfinished refuses in words instead of allow-with-nudge.\n- **Asymmetry** deliberate and argued in code: only the STARTING verb refuses; set_done keeps its nudge; set_todo untouched.\n- **Deliberate non-gates** argued at plan.ts:876: set_after onto a started node records a true discovery; capture cannot arrive blocked (verified on the schema by review).\n- **Now** (2026-08-15): Kolu terminal `bf2dbd48` (Claude Opus), branch `doing-refuses-blocked`, PR #181.\n  - Built and verified: 1655 unit, 601 e2e.\n  - Stage #review — Grok posted NITS ONLY: pin the two non-gates with planner cases; the click-away note; capture-can't-arrive-blocked verified on the schema.\n  - Sharpest question: the relocated undo scenario — what undo does restoring doing onto a now-blocked node wants its own assertion.\n  - VIDEO EVIDENCE ordered by the human.\n  - **MERGE:** PRE-APPROVED — autonomous once findings addressed + CI green at final head.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"hits-carry-custom","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a8","title":"PR: search hits carry custom properties — the lane board becomes one query","done":"2026-08-15T20:19:52-04:00","desc":"Ruled 2026-08-15 at PR #179's merge gate: hits do NOT carry custom yet (read_node does); this node is the future PR.\n\n- **What it buys:** \"every lane with pr=X\" / \"every node with source=Y\" as one search_nodes call — the orchestration board's native query.\n- **Shape:** hits gain a custom field the way they carry see/after.\n- **Open:** the wire cost of big values wants a look — hits are many, values can be long — truncate or key-only?","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/192","terminal":"48b46d55-9779-4fe7-b206-b89fe61fe87d"}}
{"id":"chat-steer-on-send","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a9","title":"PR: chat sends immediately — mid-turn messages steer the agent, the queue dies","done":"2026-08-15T20:30:07-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15 from a live freeze.\n\n- The orchestrator spawned a babysitter subagent; the ACP adapter holds a turn's settlement open while a spawned subagent lives (claude-agent-acp `turnAwaitingSubagents`/`Turn.deferredSettle`).\n- olai's queue-until-idle branch (`packages/chat/src/chat.ts` send(): `if (turn !== null) { queue.push(prompt) }`) sat on 4 user messages for the turn's whole lifetime.\n- Cancel ran `dropQueue(\"cancelled\")` and destroyed them.\n  - No copy anywhere: the transcript is not persisted, the agent session is the persistence, and a queued message never reached the session.\n- **THE FIX**, learned from how Zed's composer never locks: send the prompt immediately, always.\n  - The adapter already supports a prompt arriving mid-turn — it STEERS: the message is injected into the running turn (`steeredSettle`, the pre-emption lanes) — so a user can talk to the agent while a subagent holds the turn.\n  - The queue and its drop are DELETED, not patched.\n- **CANCEL SEMANTICS** fall out: with steer-on-send everything typed was already delivered, so cancel means stop-the-agent and nothing else.\n  - For a residual undelivered message (steer in flight at cancel), keep the row marked unsent with a resend affordance — the panel never silently destroys user words.","created":"2026-08-15T18:37:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:08:26-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/194","superseded-by-366":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: the title's \"mid-turn messages steer\" was REVERSED by #366 — sends queue at the agent by default, steering is the explicit Alt+Enter gesture (withdrawn after the session queues, pending claude-agent-acp#1039). The \"olai's own queue is deleted\" half survives: the wait moved to the agent's FIFO","terminal":"333bf4f1-ed35-48ed-8d27-de46102f1b88"}}
{"id":"chat-subagent-lanes","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"aA","title":"PR: subagent activity renders as its own lane in the chat panel","done":"2026-08-15T20:19:53-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15, the human's ask from the freeze incident (it was one of the 4 dropped queued messages, resurrected).\n\n- In-session subagent activity renders flat and unattributed — a tool call made by a spawned subagent looks exactly like the main agent's own, so subagents are invisible-yet-leaking.\n- The ACP adapter already tags subagent traffic with `_meta.claudeCode.parentToolUseId` (claude-agent-acp, `liveBackgroundTasks`); olai drops the meta on the floor between `packages/chat/src/agent.ts` and the panel.\n- **Fix:** group/attribute subagent tool frames under the Agent call that spawned them.","created":"2026-08-15T18:37:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/193","terminal":"a5cb10bc-f92d-4659-a02d-c2c2fbb2f9bf"}}
{"id":"instructions-reconcile","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"aB","title":"Retire orchestrator/instructions.md — the orchestrator's standing rules live in olai itself #human","done":"2026-08-25T16:24:51-04:00","desc":"**REFRAMED by the human 2026-08-23 ~21:05** (was: \"Update instructions.md to match how we work now\"): don't reconcile the file — RETIRE it. **DONE 2026-08-25:** every standing rule graduated to the node that owns it, and instructions.md is now a ~12-line bootstrap stub — identity, \"THE BOARD IS THE INSTRUCTIONS\" (the three-file reading order), and the memory rule. Nothing else.\n\n**Where everything went:** pipeline prose (implementation/review/CI/evidence/deferrals/approval/retire + the green-ci footnote) → dag.olai's step descs, one law per step; spawn mechanics → dag-pr-implement; kolu discipline + the watch contract + babysit/wake rules → Supervision (agents.olai, its own root — not a roster row); CI venue + kolu-PR process → Supervision's children; board protocol (ops-only writes, commit-per-beat, git verbs) + planning + item-shape + closing-keywords → the lanes root conventions; roster menu → agents-root (review steps roster-role-shaped, ir-agent-menu); evidence recipes → CLAUDE.md (the human's ruling); no-deferrals → dag-pr-deferrals + the Inbox Deferrals root. Plan doc: [brainstorming/instructions-breakdown.md](../brainstorming/instructions-breakdown.md).\n\nThe stub itself remains by design — the chat/orchestrator entry point still needs one bootstrap pointer; deleting the file outright is a separate call the human can make any day (the board wouldn't notice).","created":"2026-08-15T18:47:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:25:01-04:00","custom":{"brainstorm":"brainstorming/instructions-breakdown.md"}}
{"id":"ir-now-section","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a0","title":"Replace the \"Now\" section — done, two small fixes left","done":"2026-08-15T19:03:40-04:00","desc":"Done: the section now points at lanes.olai.\n\n- **Leftover 1:** it says lane entries are \"mirrors\" — they aren't; each lane is a real copy of the template, and the `item` property links it back to the roadmap.\n- **Leftover 2:** the deleted paragraph \"prose is not a ledger\" (anything worth tracking must be a node, not a sentence) was a good general rule — consider moving it to the Planning section instead of losing it.","created":"2026-08-15T18:47:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00"}
{"id":"ir-pipeline-prose","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a1","title":"Remove the duplicated PR-pipeline prose — dag.olai is the source","done":"2026-08-25T16:10:26-04:00","desc":"- Three sections describe the same pipeline dag.olai now defines as nodes; shorten them to a pointer.\n- Keep only what nodes can't hold: the evidence-upload steps, the check-CI-properly footnote, merge ordering, killing terminals after merge.","created":"2026-08-15T18:47:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:10:26-04:00","custom":{"keep-list-update":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: one keep-list item already graduated — \"killing terminals after merge\" is held by dag-pr-retire's desc; the three duplicating sections still stand in instructions.md"}}
{"id":"ir-babysit-split","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a2","title":"Split the terminal-watching rules: orchestrator vs chat agent","done":"2026-08-25T16:24:45-04:00","desc":"- Watching should use kolu MCP waits, not background shell loops.\n- The chat agent must never watch at all: a chat turn can't end while a helper it spawned is running (it froze the chat once). It dispatches and answers when poked.\n- Both rules become moot once olai watches terminals itself (see olai-subscribes).","created":"2026-08-15T18:47:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:24:45-04:00","custom":{"flip-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: the first bullet states the REVERSE of the ruled shape — instructions.md now makes kolu watch (a persistent background monitor) the only wake mechanism and BANS blocking MCP waits; the chat-agent-never-watches half stands"}}
{"id":"ir-ops-only-rule","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a3","title":"Outline files were hand-written once — ruled: always use the MCP tools","done":"2026-08-15T19:06:07-04:00","desc":"The doc says outlines are only ever written through olai's MCP tools. I broke that: lanes.olai and dag.olai started as hand-written files.\n\n- **Ruled:** no exceptions.\n- dag.olai was deleted and recreated properly through the tools.\n- lanes.olai stays as-is — it was hand-born but every edit since went through the tools, and recreating it would have disturbed lanes mid-work.\n- **Also seen:** a brand-new file isn't noticed by the server until touched, and a deleted one lingers briefly — the first is a real (small) bug.","created":"2026-08-15T18:47:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00"}
{"id":"ir-agent-menu","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a4","title":"List agent choices from agents.olai instead of hardcoding names","done":"2026-08-25T16:10:23-04:00","desc":"The doc hardcodes example agent names. Pull the menu from agents.olai (role=author / role=reviewer) so adding an agent is one node, not a doc edit.","created":"2026-08-15T18:47:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:10:23-04:00","custom":{"scope-widened":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: the hardcoding now also lives in dag.olai's step titles (\"review: grok\", \"review: opencode\") while the actual roster grew (pi/kimi-k3 reviewed #366) — widen the fix to both files, reading the roster from agents.olai"}}
{"id":"ir-watcher-idle-safe","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a5","title":"Fix the watch recipe for idle terminals","done":"2026-08-24T16:07:53-04:00","desc":"- `kolu debrief` in a loop works while an agent is busy, but on an idle agent it returns the same screen instantly — loop it and it spins forever.\n- Fix: first `kolu wait <id> --until working`, then the debrief loop. Document both shapes.","created":"2026-08-15T18:56:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:07:55-04:00","custom":{"resolved":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: overtaken — the debrief-loop recipe this node fixes is gone from instructions.md, and its proposed fix (a blocking kolu wait) is now BANNED by the same doc's watch ruling (kolu watch as the only wake mechanism). The idle-terminal hazard is documented on supervision-watcher instead"}}
{"id":"ir-merge-master-rule","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a6","title":"Make the merge-master rule agree across docs","done":"2026-08-24T16:07:52-04:00","desc":"- Ruled: never rebase a PR; merge master into it.\n- Left to settle: instructions.md says always merge master before CI; CLAUDE.md (and the dag template) say only on conflicts or when CI needs newer code. Pick one and make the docs agree.","created":"2026-08-15T19:00:32-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:07:53-04:00","custom":{"resolved":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: the docs now agree — instructions.md, CLAUDE.md and dag-pr-merge-master all state conflicts-only (or CI needs master)"}}
{"id":"search-props-ui","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"aD","title":"PR: search results show properties, and say when a property is why a hit came back — with an e2e test","done":"2026-08-15T21:35:10-04:00","desc":"Ruled at PR #192's gate (2026-08-15): three of that PR's leftovers fold into ONE follow-up PR, done by the same agent.\n\n- (1) The web app's search results still draw only title and place — a person can't see the properties the wire now carries.\n- (2) A hit found by prop:agent=X can't say a property is why it matched — growing `matched` an arm changes what that field means, and this PR must rule that design point.\n- (3) With something finally on screen, the e2e scenario that #192 rightly skipped becomes writable.","created":"2026-08-15T20:18:21-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/195","terminal":"48b46d55-9779-4fe7-b206-b89fe61fe87d"}}
{"id":"chat-subagent-asks","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"aE","title":"PR: a subagent's permission form names who is asking","done":"2026-08-19T10:57:20-04:00","desc":"Ruled at PR #193's gate (2026-08-15): when a subagent triggers a permission question, the form is drawn in the main column and reads as the main agent's.\n\n- The adapter already stamps parentToolUseId on session/request_permission and on a subagent's AskUserQuestion elicitation — ChatEntry.parent is tool-only and transcript.ask is never handed it.\n- **Grok's sharpening**, recorded: the unattributed row also breaks the lane stretch, so the lane re-opens and names itself again (visible, not silent).\n- The plumbing exists; recorded in packages/chat/README.md and docs/architecture.md.","created":"2026-08-15T20:18:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/0fa068bb","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/255"}}
{"id":"unsent-discriminate","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"aF","title":"PR: an unsent message says timed-out vs refused — AgentGone learns the difference","done":"2026-08-18T10:06:53-04:00","desc":"Ruled at PR #194's gate (2026-08-15): a message marked unsent after a steer timeout cannot be told apart from one refused by a dead agent.\n\n- The timeout arm is an inference; today only the honest comment at the site says so.\n- **Real fix:** discriminates answered-from-unanswered inside AgentGone so a timeout routes like a dead turn (notice, no resend button) while a refusal keeps its button.\n- Redesigns ask, a shared primitive with five call sites — a real project, which is why #194 rightly deferred it.","created":"2026-08-15T20:18:27-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00"}
{"id":"ir-evidence-recipe-reach","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a7","title":"Put the evidence-upload recipe where worker agents can see it","done":"2026-08-25T16:10:29-04:00","desc":"- The screenshot-upload recipe lives in docs/orchestrator/instructions.md, which workers never read — #195's screenshots ended up on catbox.moe.\n- Either move it to HACKING.md/CLAUDE.md, or keep including it in every dispatch briefing (the interim practice).","created":"2026-08-15T21:33:15-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:10:29-04:00"}
{"id":"ir-closing-keywords","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a8","title":"Rule: no GitHub closing keywords before a PR number in commits","done":"2026-08-25T16:10:34-04:00","desc":"- Incident: a board commit saying \"closes #202\" auto-closed that PR mid-review.\n- Add to instructions.md: in commits pushed to the default branch, never put close/fix/resolve words directly before a PR or issue number — write \"finishes #202\", or put the number first.","created":"2026-08-16T10:48:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:10:34-04:00","custom":{"retarget":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: \"add to instructions.md\" contradicts the parent's retirement reframe — per its destination map this rule belongs on the ledger root that owns commits (the roadmap roots), not the file"}}
{"id":"ir-item-shape","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a9","title":"Rule: a roadmap item is a PR, never a category","done":"2026-08-25T16:10:31-04:00","desc":"The human's rule (2026-08-16): a bare category name marked todo is meaningless. Work items get PR-shaped titles; unmarked parent bullets do the grouping. Write it into instructions.md.","created":"2026-08-16T14:32:58-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:10:31-04:00","custom":{"retarget":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: \"write it into instructions.md\" contradicts the parent's retirement reframe — the rule belongs on the roadmap roots per the destination map"}}
{"id":"ir-deferral-tag","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"aA","title":"Write into instructions.md: a deferral node wears #deferral and carries from=&lt;PR&gt; as a property","done":"2026-08-20T14:13:47-04:00","desc":"DONE 2026-08-20 on the human's word (\"do it, uncommitted\"): the sentence is in instructions.md's approval section — a deferral node wears #deferral in its TITLE and carries from=<PR> as a property; prose in the note is neither. Written through write_document; the edit sits UNCOMMITTED on disk at the human's instruction. The drift it closes: eight deferral-born nodes filed by later sessions carried only the from= property and were retro-tagged the same day (commit 7c65d8fd).","created":"2026-08-16T14:41:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T14:13:47-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-phases","parent":"j9azop3o","ord":"a2","title":"The orchestrator, phased — each PR self-sufficient, the edges are the order","desc":"The PR plan for [orchestrator.md](../brainstorming/orchestrator.md), moved here so the order is EDGES the board enforces rather than prose (`set_doing` refuses a blocked phase). **The standing rule: each PR is complete and correct on its own the day it merges — nothing deferred; the phases sequence work, never split a feature into a broken half and its fix.** The two door PRs (terminal-door, terminal-stream) live here as phases 1a and 6.","created":"2026-08-25T16:56:00-04:00"}
