{"id":"overnight-2026-08-15","parent":"day-2026-08-15","ord":"a3","title":"Overnight run, 2026-08-15 — the standing orders","desc":"Ruled by the human before bed.\n- **THE SIX:** html-images, html-frame-height, watcher-postboot-blind, suite-load-flakes (on a kolu-ci-* box), outlines-quadratic, html-memory.\n- **SCHEDULE:**\n  - 3 Opus authors max at a time (search-props-ui holds a slot until it closes).\n  - The three HTML items serialize as a chain (frame-height → images → memory) because they share code.\n  - Watcher and outlines are independent.\n  - Flakes dispatches to kolu-ci-1 when a slot frees.\n- **RULES:**\n  - grok+opencode review every PR; merges on the orchestrator's judgment.\n  - Routine leftovers are filed on the roadmap, may be dispatched as follow-ups, and the PR merges; anything needing human eyes stays OPEN with notes.\n  - suite-load-flakes may legitimately end as a diagnosis + reproducer rather than a merged PR.\n  - The Bun bump (bun-watcher-bump) stays the human's — briefed into the watcher lane.\n  - Every lane walks the dag-pr template; evidence is verified before any merge.","created":"2026-08-15T20:57:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T18:16:44-04:00"}
