{"id":"lane-sev-review-opencode","parent":"lane-search-everywhere","ord":"a3","title":"review: opencode","done":"2026-08-17T05:06:32-04:00","desc":"**Verdict:** does not object — claims hold under diff-level scrutiny.\n\n- Scope.archived as a question-level boolean correctly placed and tested at all three layers.\n- Sidebar counts from the unnarrowed agenda, filtered counts same definition as outline pages, traced through matchesIn/placesIn.\n- **Findings worth follow-up, none blocking:**\n  - (1) a page reaches archived candidates via showsArchived's tree-root scan, so its filter evaluates every archived node in the directory as a candidate — nothing extra draws but the walk is paid, leaking the \"page-derived\" claim.\n  - (2) settings/done.ts:62-65 — visibleIn always re-wraps the tree arm into a fresh object so the rows === drawn.rows identity the next line claims is never exercised; return drawn itself when withoutDone handed back the same array.\n  - (8) routes.test.ts — add a negative round-trip pin that a hand-typed ?q= on a /doc/ address is dropped, since routeOf's document arm is the only place the exclusion lives.","after":["lane-sev-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-17T03:37:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:00-04:00","custom":{"terminal":"e4fe755c-3067-40f5-86bd-be25ad2003a3"}}
