{"id":"lane-mi4-review-grok","parent":"lane-model-indices-4","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok","done":"2026-08-17T10:25:24-04:00","desc":"**Verdict:** do not object to merge.\n\n- The fold is the same patch the write gate uses, held to derive(assemble(…)).\n- The path-order landmine unified and pinned both sides.\n- Rev a two-sided contract.\n- Decline rebuilds once with a fresh revision map.\n- A retired tab never sees a second counter.\n- **Three suggestions, none a wrong view:**\n  - (1) docs/architecture.md:34 quotes 288→48 ms where the design doc and format README quote 293/51 for the same vault — reconcile.\n  - (2) deriving.bench.ts:211 — sizeOf asserts only the first frame so it wouldn't catch Solid's server build (only --conditions browser saves the bench).\n  - (3) deriving.test.ts:58 — same() omits children, mirrorsOf, edgesTo, so a fold that rebuilt/reordered those three would still pass.\n- Reviewed at 56bd1a6.","after":["lane-mi4-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-17T08:45:47-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:00-04:00","custom":{"terminal":"cd482c49-b6db-4dde-9da9-7d0ee30bc2c3"}}
{"id":"lane-mi4-review-opencode","parent":"lane-model-indices-4","ord":"a3","title":"review: opencode","done":"2026-08-17T10:39:08-04:00","desc":"**Verdict:** do not object to merge — \"the tightest slice of the four\".\n\n- Adversarial probes against the actual fold (out-of-order, coalesced, churn, decline, empty-first-frame, leak) all pass.\n- The bench's two ways to lie are throw-not-number; numbers reproduce.\n- The landmine pinned from three directions with a property test generating the pathological pair.\n- **Findings:**\n  - (1) **BUG**, format/src/dates.ts:432 — dailyNotesOn still sorts by Order.String while the sidebar now uses byPath, so a day page lists 2026-08-17.md before 2026-08-17/… where everything else reads the pair the other way.\n  - (2) suggestion, deriving.test.ts:58 — same() compares 7 of 10 indexes, omitting children/mirrorsOf/edgesTo at the client seam (matches grok's #3).\n  - (3) suggestion, deriving.ts:104-112 — a new empty/broken file enters the fold one frame later than the publisher's literal upsert; harmless but the one provable divergence and the header comment doesn't name it.\n  - (4) suggestion — the no-fold-across-two-rev-counters guarantee rests on the identity handshake and nothing points at the_connection.feature as its executable half.\n  - (5) note — the O(files) remove-diff only runs when counts say something left; kept fast-path works as written.\n- Reviewed at 56bd1a6.","after":["lane-mi4-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-17T08:45:47-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:00-04:00","custom":{"terminal":"5d40711d-380b-459c-8203-5c0b65e66213"}}
