{"id":"lane-obv-review-grok","parent":"lane-olai-batch-verbs","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok","done":"2026-08-17T11:56:18-04:00","desc":"**Verdict:** do not object to merge — no correctness hole in atomicity, the fold/refusal-identity claim, the #207 gate, forward-ref/cycle naming, or rev-once.\n\n- **Six findings, all test/doc:**\n  - (1) batch.test.ts:281 — no apply that creates a child then marks the parent done, so the #207 message-identity claim is unpinned on the sequence that changes what the gate sees.\n  - (2) ops.test.ts:785 — the halfway-refusal test's op 3 doesn't depend on derived state ops 1–2 changed (the sharp atomicity case is untested).\n  - (3) writing.ts:81 — create_outline's seed schema takes props/see/waitsOn but the advertised seed sentence lists the old closed field set.\n  - (4) writing.ts:160 — a child-level after:[\"id\"] is silently dropped, and the waitsOn/after bend makes that footgun likely — refuse or honor it.\n  - (5) tools.ts:519 — apply's \"the set is re-read between ops\" overclaims (the fold never re-reads the directory).\n  - (6) plan.ts:1258 — heldUp's new paragraph narrates branch history instead of the rule.\n- Reviewed at the refactor head.","after":["lane-obv-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-17T10:45:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:01-04:00","custom":{"terminal":"f8e60118-3863-49f8-bb55-e564f1d120b4"}}
{"id":"lane-obv-review-opencode","parent":"lane-olai-batch-verbs","ord":"a3","title":"review: opencode","done":"2026-08-17T12:04:11-04:00","desc":"**Verdict:** do not object on design or correctness — but asks finding 1 fixed or documented BEFORE merge.\n\n- The fold is exact (could not make batch and sequential semantics diverge).\n- Atomicity disk-proven; loops named in the single verb's words; layering fix genuinely re-caps patch; prose to house standard.\n- **Findings:**\n  - (1) **BUG**, writing.ts:786 — update has no `was` and decoding drops it silently, so an agent migrating from set_title/set_desc loses the conditional-write guard while believing it still holds.\n  - (2) bug (comment wrong, code right), plan.ts:651 — the wiring-after-emit comment claims a false crash justification; the true reason is refusal priority.\n  - (3) suggestion — \"sixteen verbs\" prose vs seventeen batched verbs.\n  - (12) prose judgment: the three descriptions carry the waitsOn/after bend honestly, only the missing `was` sentence gaps them.\n  - (13) observation — plan.ts:670 door two reads capturesOpenWork(request) not post-wiring records, exact today only because no pass re-marks; wants a guard comment.\n- Reviewed at the refactor head.","after":["lane-obv-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-17T10:45:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:01-04:00","custom":{"terminal":"c8e4fe67-de90-4822-a9fc-f7a08351c1a9"}}
