{"id":"lane-kolu-one-shot-submit","parent":"day-2026-08-17","ord":"aE","title":"kolu-one-shot-submit","done":"2026-08-18T10:07:38-04:00","desc":"**CLOSED NOT MERGED** — PR #2177 closed by the human's ruling 2026-08-18 after three rounds of live field testing.\n\n- Full reason on the PR and post-mortem on the roadmap node (kolu-one-shot-submit, back to todo).\n- **Root cause:** the quiet-conjunct starved forever on grok's ~1s idle repaint.\n- **Fix direction:** the successor must gate on adapter agent-state, not byte silence.\n- Branch one-shot-submit preserved; author + reviewers + test terminals all retired.\n- The merge steps' marks removed (they never happened and never will).","created":"2026-08-17T10:45:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T18:16:45-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","ci":"181eda48 (master merged, incl. #2179's reaper): CI running. Field-report-#2 fix in at f342319e — \"agent\" readiness accepts recognized-session-not-working OR foreground-process-is-a-known-agent-command (node-pty process name, exists at exec), quiet conjunct kept; bash still refuses. AgentAdapter grew commandName (each adapter's own literal, now readable); agentAdapters.ts the single import site. The e2e fixture PAIR now covers refusal AND happy path via MOCK_PROCESS_NAME (author measured node-pty reports process.title verbatim first). Author owned the shipped-past-flag lapse. Local: typecheck+lint clean, all units, e2e 7/7 on fresh pu box. Held unmerged.","for-morning":"Held for your word, everything else done. Residual decision: on darwin, an agent installed at a deep path can have its process name truncated (measured: 16-char ps limit) and be refused a first message — safe direction, documented; the author OFFERS the proper fix (plumb the shell's preexec hint — shim-robust, platform-independent) rather than leaving a comment. Take the offer, or merge as-is?","repo":"repo-kolu"}}
