{"id":"lane-kos-review-grok","parent":"lane-kolu-one-shot-submit","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok","done":"2026-08-17T13:55:12-04:00","desc":"**Verdict:** OBJECT to merge.\n\n- **Bugs:**\n  - (1) website mcp.mdx:129 still teaches the three-step ritual as the only path, and no changelog entry.\n  - (2) kolu-mcp/sendInput.ts:355 — `typed` is phase===\"settle\", so a GONE terminal is reported as text still sitting in a box that no longer exists.\n  - (3) padi/submitInput.ts:259 — abort ignored when the prompt is already idle, so a cancelled call types and then refuses-at-settle.\n  - (4) mockAgentTui.mjs:88 — hold-back misses the 5-byte END prefix \\x1b[201, a split before ~ leaks the marker.\n  - (5) kolu-mcp/create.ts:317 — a create-message failure always says \"dispatch with submit:true\", which double-types a settle-phase residue (must land in the same pass).\n- **Suggestions:**\n  - (6) CLI message without run/argv types the brief into the shell and presses Enter.\n  - (7) surface.ts:947 — 5s first-message quiet window can read a real agent's boot silence as an idle prompt.\n  - (8) blank --message refused in code, missing from the blank-flag table.\n  - (9) padi-tui create never grew --message (face parity).\n- **Grok's close:** the boundary/5.3/control-leg/CLI-retype/apm discipline are in good shape; the refusal story is unfinished until the structured recovery matches the residue, and the docs must stop teaching the replaced path.\n- Reviewed at 1275eecc.","after":["lane-kos-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-17T10:45:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:01-04:00","custom":{"terminal":"d729df56-1ccc-44d9-8dd4-e063743d041b"}}
{"id":"lane-kos-review-opencode","parent":"lane-kolu-one-shot-submit","ord":"a3","title":"review: opencode","done":"2026-08-17T14:01:09-04:00","desc":"**Verdict:** no objection to merge — every probeable claim held under adversarial inspection.\n\n- Refusal phases exhaustive and truthful.\n- Marker holdback survives exhaustive split probing.\n- Additive-minor contract correct both directions.\n- sendInput/submitInput boundary consistent across all three faces.\n- e2e demonstrates the destructive failure.\n- **Findings:** one doc nit, one guidance clause, one theoretical docstring overreach, one optional create knob (submitTimeoutMs) — none blocking.\n- Notes the red x86_64 unit check as a pre-existing grok flake outside the diff.\n- **NOTE:** factually contradicts grok's bugs 2/3/4 (phase-on-gone, abort-when-idle, END-prefix holdback) — the author must adjudicate each with a reproducing test, not pick a reviewer.\n- Reviewed at 1275eecc.","after":["lane-kos-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-17T10:45:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:01-04:00","custom":{"terminal":"938bea2c-0039-4750-bb90-4b42c0fb480f"}}
