{"id":"lane-kos-ci","parent":"lane-kolu-one-shot-submit","ord":"a6","title":"CI green at head — both platforms","done":"2026-08-17T18:26:56-04:00","desc":"GREEN — the seven red runs were never this branch.\n- **Fix:** `sudo killall fseventsd` on petit took the box from 58 MB free to 11.2 GB free; darwin lane went green on the very next run with no code change — first fully green run in seven attempts.\n- **Head:** caa20425 on one-shot-submit, master an ancestor, all reviews' findings addressed, every required check green.\n- **Consequences (author-recorded):**\n  - kolu #2175 answered: watcher tests and their 3s budget were correct all along, so #2176's darwin skip is now suspect and worth retiring.\n  - #2178 stands as the real defect since the daemon-lifetime leak will refill that box.\n- **OWED on petit** (unrelated to this PR): `sudo launchctl limit maxfiles 65536 524288` — the untouched 256-descriptor limit is the prime suspect for wedging kaval into orphans.\n- **Noted:** darwin resolved 4 workers against a cap of 6 (sizes on available memory); first run post-restart — worth re-reading next green run to see if it climbs.","after":["lane-kos-merge-master","lane-kos-address"],"created":"2026-08-17T10:45:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:19-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-kos-evidence","parent":"lane-kolu-one-shot-submit","ord":"a7","title":"evidence verified","done":"2026-08-17T18:27:02-04:00","desc":"Verified — feature proven three ways.\n- **Unit tests:** over the predicate and the four-step sequence.\n- **E2E:** five proofs against a real padi driving real PTYs, green on BOTH platforms.\n  - Includes the settle-phase-staged leg (text on screen, unsubmitted, one Enter delivers exactly once).\n  - Includes a control leg demonstrating the &lt;&lt;CLEARED:\"LOST-MESSAGE\"&gt;&gt; destruction the design prevents.\n- **VHS:** recording of the real binary showing all four beats.\n- **Reviews:** both recorded — grok objected twice, satisfied on the third pass; opencode never objected.\n- **Self-corrections volunteered (not hidden):**\n  - A speculative fix to someone else's test, reverted after it proved a misdiagnosis.\n  - A CI note retracted when \"the linux lane is green every time\" stopped being true.","after":["lane-kos-ci"],"created":"2026-08-17T10:45:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:19-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-kos-deferrals","parent":"lane-kolu-one-shot-submit","ord":"a8","title":"deferrals ruled — in-PR unless strong reason","done":"2026-08-17T18:27:06-04:00","desc":"Nothing deferred from the PR itself — all findings from both reviewers addressed in-PR.\n- **Filed elsewhere** (per the author's own judgment and the human's ratification):\n  - The darwin upgrade-window flake — its own kolu issue, after the author's first fix attempt proved a misdiagnosis and was reverted.\n  - #2178 (daemon reaping not doing what it promises) — corroborated by the linux dial.test.ts red.\n- **FOR THE HUMAN**, unrelated to the PR:\n  - Run `sudo launchctl limit maxfiles 65536 524288` on petit.\n  - Revisit #2176's darwin skip now that fseventsd's restart proved the watcher budget was correct.","after":["lane-kos-evidence"],"created":"2026-08-17T10:45:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:19-04:00"}
