{"id":"lane-sp-review-grok2","parent":"lane-second-pane","ord":"a6","title":"review: grok","done":"2026-08-17T14:00:42-04:00","desc":"**Verdict:** OBJECT to merge — issues 1 and 2 are user-visible breaks of stated pane principles (full review /tmp/grok-1000/grok-review-ce84887a.md).\n- **Bugs:**\n  - (1) router.tsx:241 — narrow-screen tabs snapshot the pane index: content does not switch and close can throw.\n  - (2) workspace.ts:263 — Alt+click reuse of a collapsed right neighbour leaves a rail that will not expand.\n  - (3) Palette.tsx:515 — lone-page Alt+Arrow preventDefault swallows word-motion/Back.\n- **Suggestions:**\n  - (4) second_pane.feature misses exactly the cases that would have caught bugs 1–3.\n  - (5) pane/crossing.ts is a design-history comment file duplicating the brainstorm doc.\n  - (6) faces.tsx:144 — two panes of the SAME .md share heading ids and scrollIntoView moves the first copy in DOM order, not the navigating pane — resolve under the pane's own root.\n  - (7) second-pane.md:49 overclaims dismissal isolation (topmost.ts is one page-wide ticket order — the right rule, wrongly described) and documents palette/header-search Alt+click that isn't wired (runItem always props.go).\n- Reviewed at aaf94588.","after":["lane-sp-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-17T13:27:51-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:19-04:00","custom":{"terminal":"3c24e30d-77d8-442d-a755-a82d78d3fa08"}}
