{"id":"lane-xyne-review-opencode2","parent":"lane-xyne-ts-client","ord":"a2","title":"round 2 review: opencode (re-verdict, posts PR comment)","done":"2026-08-17T18:17:49-04:00","desc":"**Round 2 verdict:** DO NOT OBJECT — posted as PR comment https://github.com/juspay/xyne-boxes/pull/24#issuecomment-5320901421.\n- All three blockers genuinely fixed, not half-fixed; checked exactly the half-fix shapes it was warned about:\n  - Checksums are COMPARED not merely fetched.\n  - The install is tmp-then-mv within BIN_DIR with a test proving a corrupt update preserves the working binary.\n  - Signal deaths map to 128+n with a live `kill -s TERM $$` test asserting 143.\n- Both declines accepted as internally consistent with an owner: (8) opentui kept on an explicit product call; (11) version stays diagnostic exit-0.\n- Calls the Auth union → discriminated-union change a real P4 improvement.\n- **Non-blocking nit:** the installer's COMMIT-file fallback path has no test coverage anywhere (install.test.sh pins XYNE_BOXES_COMMIT for hermeticity, so install.sh:88-93 is never exercised).","after":["lane-xyne-address"],"created":"2026-08-17T17:43:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:19-04:00","custom":{"terminal":"f270d083-b157-4b3e-86b4-9f04a654d6c2"}}
{"id":"lane-xyne-review-opus","parent":"lane-xyne-ts-client","ord":"a3","title":"round 2 review: claude opus — the human's addition, posts PR comment","done":"2026-08-17T18:24:17-04:00","desc":"**Verdict:** do not object to merge, but 17 findings and four it would fix before announcing the installer — posted https://github.com/juspay/xyne-boxes/pull/24#issuecomment-5320957049.\n- **Read cold and VERIFIED BY RUNNING:** bun test 37 pass, tsc clean, install.sh driven against a local file:// release through first-install, reinstall, partial-failure, read-only-dest, missing-checksums, pre-existing-pu.\n- Confirms the two hardest things are right: checksum compared; signal death → 128+n with a real SIGTERM'd child.\n- **The four it would fix:**\n  - (1) BUG ssh.ts:150-151 — user -o options appended AFTER the client's own and ssh takes the first value.\n    - So `connect box -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes` is silently ignored; the bash client put user args first — a silent parity regression.\n    - Two-line swap, confirmed by running sshArgv.\n  - (2) install.sh:101-105 — verification atomic per asset but NOT across the install: a failing step leaves xyne-boxes+pu installed, no step, no PATH line, and the binary's hint points back at the same failing installer.\n  - (3) cli.ts:13-19 — every parse error prints twice.\n  - (4) site/index.html never mentions the curl installer — the headline feature is undiscoverable.\n- **Also confirmed empirically:**\n  - `ln -sfn` destroys a pre-existing ~/.local/bin/pu.\n  - Rosetta's uname -m makes a supported Mac report \"unsupported platform\".\n- **TEST-HONESTY:** gaps line up exactly with findings 1 and 2 (ssh.test.ts never passes options.sshArgs; install.test.sh corrupts only the first asset), so BOTH bugs pass the suite.\n- **DISAGREES with opencode on two points:**\n  - Its proxy-message fix traded one wrong audience for the other (xyne-boxes connect isn't on PATH under the documented nix run path).\n  - Its claim that ssh options \"all carry over from the bash client\" is contradicted by finding 1.","after":["lane-xyne-address"],"created":"2026-08-17T17:43:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:19-04:00","custom":{"terminal":"e7178d20-bfd3-4e2e-8c01-6789910d72a4"}}
{"id":"lane-xyne-address2","parent":"lane-xyne-ts-client","ord":"a4","title":"address round-2 findings","done":"2026-08-19T18:14:57-04:00","desc":"**ROUND 3:** both verdicts in, both do-not-object.\n- **Opencode:** do-not-object on the addressed head (posted).\n- **Claude Opus:** no objection — ship it, at 0e0792c — comment 5321161941; mutation-proved every testable fix, ran all four blockers live.\n- **Residuals flagged:**\n  - R1: ssh ordering over-corrected — user -o now beats hardened MACs; parity = split identityArgs/policyArgs.\n  - R5: site installer's COMMIT asset named a ts-only commit — the author's 860b56e raw-URL switch speaks to it.\n- **Since then the human drives the author directly:**\n  - 860b56e (raw nightly-tag installer URL).\n  - 3c28080 (Effect beta.103 → rc.110, 43 tests green).\n  - Plus advisory Q&A (nix packaging split, CI workflow split — both proposed, not applied).\n- **BOTH REVIEWER TERMINALS RETIRED** by the human 2026-08-17 ~19:20 (e7178d20, f270d083 gone; the staged \"fix R1 and R2\" died unsubmitted with e7178d20).\n- Step stays doing until the human's residual pass concludes and a final head exists.","after":["lane-xyne-review-opencode2","lane-xyne-review-opus"],"created":"2026-08-17T17:43:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:19-04:00"}
