{"id":"lane-e2e-scratch","parent":"day-2026-08-20","ord":"a2","title":"olai — e2e shares one scratch corpus per feature where files are disjoint (Grok; reviewer opencode)","done":"2026-08-20T11:12:43-04:00","desc":"Dispatched 2026-08-20 09:5x on the human's word. Brief: scratchpad briefs/e2e-scratch-sharing.md (+ common.md).\n- The roadmap's census (555/875 @scratch) predates the ~150-scenario cut; the brief's first artefact is a fresh census table in the PR body, then per-FEATURE per-WORKER scratch servers where scenarios' files are verifiably disjoint, with a loud refusal when two sharing scenarios touch one file.\n- Evidence: before/after e2e wall time + server spawn count, underload.sh census before/after, CI green.\n\n`pr` (as written, pre-typing): #281 merged 232c1f8b7 (squash 11:11 on the human's 10:27 approval; head 5782f130, 9/9 required, opencode re-verdict do-not-object)","created":"2026-08-20T09:57:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T18:17:03-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","approval":"the human approved #281 at 10:27 — gate open; pipeline still to finish (refactor passes → opencode review → findings → CI → evidence → deferrals filed) before the squash","finding":"the roadmap's premise failed: the_agent (76) is NOT file-disjoint (same outlines + server/XDG conversation state), and the UI-edit families all mutate one outline — fresh census 490/720 @scratch, share pool ≈ 21 scenarios total. Value question for the human at the deferrals gate: merge +553 lines of harness for a 3% spawn cut, or not.","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/232c1f8b7da8146af324027bc7a917ccccbb7087","merged":"2026-08-20T11:11:31-04:00","opencode-reverdict":"do not object at 5782f130 — both new pins verified, CI 15/15 green — https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/281#issuecomment-5357810657","opencode-verdict":"OBJECTS narrowly — the restart-under-share refusal (hooks.ts:545–551), the mechanism's safety valve, is the one new behaviour without a test; one pin settle