{"id":"lane-search-saved","parent":"day-2026-08-20","ord":"a3","title":"olai — saved searches: name a pinned query where the thought arrives (Opus; reviewers grok + opencode)","done":"2026-08-20T11:53:51-04:00","desc":"Dispatched 2026-08-20 10:0x on the human's word; reviewers both grok and opencode (the human's word mid-dispatch). Brief: scratchpad briefs/search-saved.md (+ common.md).\n- The orchestrator's reading, put in the brief: Pins already settled the roadmap node's one design question (vault node, not client pref) and shipped \"get it back with one click\" — ⌘⇧P / ⌘K / ••• pin the narrowed page WITH its query. What is missing is NAMING at pin time: today a name is a markdown-link title you type by opening Pins.olai. The lane closes that slice through the same op (the pin node's title becomes `[name](address)`; rename = set_title), no new field/record/op, MCP and web consistent.\n- Visual gate applies: boot shot, name prompt, named pin on the shelf with its query, the narrowed page after clicking it.\n\n`pr` (as written, pre-typing): #282 merged fae7a1446 (squash 11:55 on the human's approval; head 92a8d4f, 9/9 required, grok + opencode do-not-object, findings addressed)\n\n`reviewer` (as written, pre-typing): grok + opencode","created":"2026-08-20T10:05:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T18:17:03-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","approval":"the human approved #282 at 11:23 and pushed a commit of their own to the branch (pins a created:today search); gate open — finishing both reviews, findings, CI at the final head, then squash","grok-verdict":"do not object — ran the pins feature 16/16 + palette_actions + drag/scroll scenarios; one-op/ask-before-write/×/undo verified; hover fix read against Pin.tsx; refactor commits converge on one Opened value; agrees with both skipped /simplify findings; docs and six shots match — https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/282#issuecomment-5358077198","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/fae7a1446b443b