{"id":"campaign-2026-08-21","parent":"day-2026-08-21","ord":"aM","title":"campaign 2026-08-21 overnight — the six #next items to Opus[1m], 3 authors at a time, grok+opencode review, auto-merge on visual evidence; one-search-box held for the human","done":"2026-08-22T14:03:16-04:00","desc":"The human's standing orders, verbatim intent: \"Dispatch #next items to Claude Opus, auto-merging them overnight autonomously upon visual evidence. Max 3 Claude's at a time can be running. Leave one-search-box unmerged for me to review tomorrow morning.\" Plus: both grok and opencode as reviewers; Opus launches with the 1M context (`opus[1m]`). No kolu-ci-* tonight — CI runs on localhost (the odu-venue ruling on supervision-watcher).\n\n**Dispatch order** (biggest first so they are ready by morning; the two bugs last, they are small): wave 1 = one-search-box, opencode-pr2, vault-level-settings; queue = identity-avatar-ladder, manifest-fold-skew, plain-estimate-nested-emphasis — each dispatched as a slot frees (a slot frees when a lane's author is retired, not when it reports).\n\n**Every lane walks the dag-pr template** (children below, cloned). Evidence is verified by the orchestrator's own eyes (the image read) before any merge. After each merge: kill the lane's terminals (author + both reviewers) as a separate step, remove the worktree, `git pull` here, and dispatch the next queued item.\n\n**Morning report owed to the human:** per lane — merged sha or why not; deferrals filed (Inbox, from=PR); anything left open; the one-search-box PR link for their review.","created":"2026-08-21T21:56:27-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T18:17:04-04:00","custom":{"briefs":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-srid-code-olai/068e8f5c-9f9e-4b56-84fb-92cfe346c225/scratchpad/briefs/ (night2-common.md + one per lane)","cap":"3 Opus authors concurrently; reviewers do not count","ci":"olai PRs: odu on localhost, Linux only (`nix run github:juspay/odu -- run --platform x86_64-linux --host x86_64-linux=localhost`), serialized across lanes by flock /tmp/olai-odu-localhost.lock; once per PR after the review round. KOLU PRs (the human's word 2026-08-21 ~22:10): BOTH platforms — the command is `nix run ./ci#odu -- run --host x86_64-linux=localhost` (kolu's odu lives in its ci/ flake, NOT `.#odu` — learned 03:49 from the kuh lane's failed eval) with no --platform, so aarch64-darwin runs on ci@petit from ~/.config/odu/hosts.json; green means every required check on both lanes.","merge-policy":"orchestrator auto-merges on: both reviews addressed, CI green at head (gh pr checks --required), visual evidence verified by eye. EXCEPTION one-search-box: fielded to the human, never auto-merged. Deferrals overnight: fold unless godly; a godly one files to the Inbox from=<PR> and is flagged in the morning report, not asked at night (the 2026-08-16 precedent).","morning-report":"WRITTEN 04:48, 2026-08-22. MERGED (7 PRs, all grok+opencode do-not-object or objection lifted, CI green, evidence eye-verified): olai #335 vault-level-settings 524e9086 · #337 identity-avatar-ladder 3d45ff08 · #336 opencode-pr2 3bf9ce9f (opencode's OBJECT lifted by a fresh re-verdict; the must-fix assertions found a real idle-over-a-live-turn bug, fixed) · #338 manifest-fold-skew 950d7625 · #339 plain-estimate-nested-emphasis 7a2a4f62 · #340 new-file-bare-name 6b464c99 · #341 bundle-reserved-prefix 0f1aab2c (determination + corrected claim: a vault's index.html was NEVER shadowed, only assets/ is) · kolu#2197 855df636 (surface-app build takes the asset prefix; both platforms) · kolu#2196 58c68bdf (upgradeHeaders allowlist; both platforms). HELD FOR THE HUMAN: #334 one-search-box at acdb4ee — reviews folded, CI green, evidence verified, SEVEN assumptions in the PR body (⌘K opens the palette and hands off rather than focusing the box; a loud 200/2000 cap instead of 'uncapped'; Shortlist.tsx kept as the picker primitive; widen pushes history; 'elsewhere' wording; Enter widens; /search rows are links); author terminal 6fc30332 parked + muted. INBOX for the human: forwarded-for-fold-spelling (kolu#2196's one godly deferral), bundle-prefix-consumer + upgrade-headers-consumer (two olai follow-ups, both unblocked by ONE kolu npins bump past 58c68bdf), the reserved-word question on olai's own routes (/media/ shadows like /assets/ did — named in bundle-reserved-prefix's desc, a new node if wanted). ASSUMPTIONS per merged PR are in each PR body's Assumptions section and on each lane's deferrals step. FLAKES seen tonight under load: lock.test.ts ENOENT, runtime.test.ts 5000ms timeout, shutdown.test SIGINT timing, zoom_and_navigate scroll-restoration — all re-ran green; worth a flake node if they recur. INCIDENTS: the watch died once (padi socket transport timeout ~02:58) and was re-armed in two minutes; the kolu odu command is `nix run ./ci#odu` (the briefs said .#odu — fixed on the board). All lane terminals, worktrees and branches retired except the parked #334.","queue":"after wave 1 (osb, oc2, vls): identity-avatar-ladder → manifest-fold-skew → plain-estimate-nested-emphasis → kolu-upgrade-headers (kolu repo) → bundle-reserved-prefix → new-file-bare-name (the human's 22:05 bug report) — the two Inbox deferrals added on the human's word ~21:57. Small bugs may jump ahead of the kolu/upstream lanes when a slot frees, to keep three authors busy.","reviewers":"grok AND opencode on every PR (the human's word), as splits of the author's terminal","ruled":"the human 2026-08-21 ~21:50, in chat","slot-rule":"a PARKED author (pipeline complete, PR fielded to the human, terminal alive only to answer the human) does not hold one of the three slots — ruled by the orchestrator 01:14 so the cap counts working authors; the human may overrule in the morning"}}
