{"id":"lane-scli-k2-green","parent":"lane-scli","ord":"aA","title":"#354 + kolu#2207 — the surface CLI rebuilt to the 2026-08-23 rulings (resumed author; grok review; the human approves both)","done":"2026-08-23T16:29:18-04:00","desc":"`dispatched` (as written, pre-typing): 2026-08-23 12:45 after /compact; both PRs to green with the five child nodes implemented; the human approves each before merging\n\nTerminal history: 114fcdf3 — claude --model opus[1m] --resume 61286578-47b6-4686-89c6-e2e53c5ae702 in a recreated .worktrees/surface-cli (detached at master); kolu worktree cli-override intact.","created":"2026-08-23T12:05:03-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T20:14:52-04:00","custom":{"approval-354":"the human 2026-08-23 16:40: #354 approved once CI is green at the final head (the prior green was at e0134fe8; the head is e88e97c4 after the docs fold + video). CI dispatched 16:40; the orchestrator merges on the green report.","approval-gate-354":"the human 2026-08-23 16:15: #354 is approved once VISUAL evidence (gif/video) is confirmed in the PR — a playing recording of the CLI in use (--help, a capture with the one-line output + --json, the --url refusal, the row appearing on the Inbox page). Relayed to the author 16:15; the orchestrator verifies the video plays and shows what it claims before calling it confirmed.","approved-2207":"the human 2026-08-23 14:55: kolu#2207 is APPROVED as of head 06f344d1 (the help layout + --json/--input + nullable flags + the override keywords) \"unless it receives new substantial commits\" — i.e. the orchestrator merges it once its CI is green on both platforms at that head (or a head that differs only by non-substantial commits: fixes the author must report); any substantial new commit re-fields it.","brief":"briefs/scli-354.md","ci-2207":"15:10 at 06f344d1: darwin 24 ok; Linux 22 ok / 2 failed — ci::home-manager (VM test kolu-adoption-currency, padi autosave cleared an empty session; not this PR's path) and ci::daemon (failed while a 16-min e2e ran on the same box) — both rerunning on a quiet box, queued behind olai's run; same failure on a quiet box → stop, the human's call. olai #354: Linux 10/10 GREEN at f4a559f9 (pre-merge); the merge commit e0134fe8 running.","ci-round-2":"15:21: three nodes rerunning on a quiet box — kolu ci::daemon + ci::home-manager (the VM autosave flake; both passed at e78a65b) and olai e2e on the merge commit e0134fe8 (1/881: archived_only_in_trash.feature:50 \"A row put away leaves the day it was scheduled for\" — passed at f4a559f9 which carried every line of the diff; the only difference is master's #355 merged in; the diff touches nothing in the trash/day path — a third data point on today's trash/agenda flakes, see Inbox/flaky tests). Author misused `odu rerun` on settled runs once, corrected to `odu run <recipe>`. Same failure on a quiet box → stop, the human's call.","dispatched":"2026-08-23T12:45:00-04:00","final":"#354 @ e88e97c4 (docs fold + the video; CI green at e0134fe8, the two commits since are docs/comment + body-only), MERGEABLE, draft; kolu#2207 merged 82518c4c; awaiting the human's approval word","kolu-2207":"12:36: kolu#2207 fully GREEN at e78a65b — 56/56 checks, both platforms (unit 4m47s, daemon 12m16s reruns on a quiet box); OPEN, DRAFT, MERGEABLE; held for the human's approval; #354's kolu-side work (help layout) lands on this branch before it merges","merged-2207":"kolu#2207 squash-merged 15:49 as 82518c4c — the human's 14:55 approval at head 06f344d1, head unchanged, every ci:: context green on both platforms after the quiet-box reruns (unit 3.3× faster on a quiet box; daemon, home-manager, and olai's e2e all green on rerun). #354 next: grok review → fold → the human.","progress":"12:15: ci::e2e GREEN on the 3rd run (dragSelectText did not recur); the real blocker was ci::unit — collectionDeltas.test.ts 'holds open for an a… is upserted' (#1681), failed twice / passed once, 12/12 in isolation, load-shaped (box at ~34 from the e2e node's own workers) — ci::daemon depends on unit and never posts while unit is red (now a verified fact, not an inference). Author confessed it ran 18 vitest invocations while the e2e node was live (against 'stay off the box') and two unsound pgrep checks; the unit+daemon rerun now has the box alone. Docs task in parallel: worktree surface-docs cut, docs/surface.md written and linked (README, index, running, architecture); website section, --help golden and transcript verification wait for the box.","report-1":"14:39 — both implemented, pushed, CI in flight. kolu#2207 @ 06f344d1 (retitled — no longer two keywords): the help-page layout (surfaceHelp, groups, examples, unlisting, build-time refusal of a stale group), the output flag with --input as the input hatch, no TTY detection, endpoint.streaming:false, `<scalar> | null` flags take the plain value with the word null to clear; 69 tests. olai #354 @ f4a559f9 pinned to it: the CLI speaks MCP to /mcp (same protocol, path, admission rule — nothing widened), --url required with nothing underneath, captured-by read from the identity header and stamped by the server, every answer names the vault (root from the server, url from the client), a write prints one line, --json the record, --help is the documentation. REMOTE PROOF against the human's vault: one capture (id bjx3jlui, rev 18) read back by search_nodes + read_node over the same --url, no bearer needed (the proxy forwards from loopback); captured-by ABSENT on that row because the deployed vault runs the pre-PR build (its answer lacks root too) — attribution proven against a branch server (curl + two route tests) and will appear on deploy. POST /capture stays deleted. Costs stated: watch/--follow gone; writer `cli` retired — a terminal's commits are /mcp's, git log cannot tell a typed line from an agent's call. Self-corrections: the identity-storage concurrency test over-claimed (fixed to what it proves); pending.test.ts flurry failed once under another lane's load, 3/3 alone. CI: kolu darwin green on petit; olai Linux in e2e on localhost; kolu Linux queued (odu: one run per checkout).","review-354":"grok DO-NOT-OBJECT at e0134fe8/4b5382b8 (16:07) — transport verified literally an MCP client of /mcp (admission, identity via proxy only, clientInfo olai-surface-cli unused for the writer); --url required everywhere (socket gone); captured-by server-stamped/absent/refused, pinned; root+url on every answer; help pinned; watch subtracted honestly. No musts. Shoulds = one theme: eight stale cli-writer/socket sentences in files the PR edited + the body's stale pin citation + running.md's `list` example missing --url. Two notable findings: production /mcp composes as chat-agent (serve.ts:211) so a typed line records as chat-agent there; grok recommends a distinct writer LATER via clientInfo.name mapping (no new door) — for the human. Killed 16:10 after posting.","reviewers":"grok (opencode dead on its key)","ruled":"the human 2026-08-23 12:00: 'Resume that agent. Have it take kolu#2207 to green CI and wait for my approval' — the orchestrator had retired the author after #352 merged, reading the 10:58 approval as covering both merges; the human wants to approve #2207 on green","state-at-resume":"e78a65b: 54 green, ci::e2e@x86_64-linux FAILED (dragSelectText ×2), ci::daemon@x86_64-linux never posted; PR still a draft","terminal":"114fcdf3","video-verified":"16:35 by the orchestrator (scratchpad/ev354/demo.mp4, 52.9 s, real mp4, frame-extracted): the friendly --help page (purpose, grouped verbs, --url/--json prose, the exit-code sentence) ✔; a capture printing `captured into /tmp/olai-demo/vault — http://127.0.0.1:7799/#2wvfa8aa` ✔; --json noted with root+url ✔; the --url-required beat ✔; the browser Inbox page with the captured rows appearing live ('fit the brass hinges — captured from a terminal, while this page was open', Inbox count 3) ✔. Embedded on its own bare line in the PR body (renders a player)."}}
