{"id":"campaign-flakes-overnight","parent":"day-2026-08-23","ord":"a4","title":"campaign 2026-08-23 overnight — resolve ALL flaky tests (Grok authors) after #358 lands","done":"2026-08-24T09:54:56-04:00","after":["lane-caa-merge"],"created":"2026-08-23T20:59:32-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T09:55:00-04:00","custom":{"lock-sequencing":"ORCHESTRATOR'S OVERNIGHT RULING 22:03 (no-questions night): #361's analysis shows lock.test.ts's only observed CI failure is the boot-listen wait child.testlib.ts owns — the exact thing #359 fixes. The lock lane therefore WAITS for #359's merge and then pins lock.test.ts on top of master (reproduce first; if a residue remains beyond #359's fix, treat it fresh). Avoids duplicating #359 in a second worktree and the merge conflict that buys. Wave 3 = e2e-load now; lock last","merge-ruling":"ORCHESTRATOR'S OVERNIGHT RULING 23:05 (no-questions night, auditable in the morning): a campaign flake-lane PR whose diff is TEST-ONLY merges despite a red combined check when (a) every CI leg containing its changed files is green on BOTH platforms, and (b) the red legs are confined to scenarios the campaign's own ledger already names (the e2e load class / petit-cold), on files the PR does not touch. Reasoning: the box stays deliberately loaded all night by the e2e-load lane's own stress reproduction — requiring quiet-box e2e green would deadlock the campaign behind the flakes it exists to kill. Admin-merge, each application recorded on its lane. First applied: #361","outcome":"COMPLETE 09:55 2026-08-24 — all five ledgered flakes resolved in five merged PRs (#359 serve, #360 pending incl. the index.lock PRODUCT race, #361 reaper, #363 e2e class incl. TWO product landing races, #364 lock gone-via-#359 + residue), every one: Grok author, opencode review with 0 MUSTs, ≥20-run loaded pin, dual-venue CI where the box allowed; 3 product bugs fixed in total, plus a 4th (@olai/log findLogfmt) from a review NIT. New ledger entries born overnight for morning triage: menu-actions-test-flaky, loglevel-test-stoppedwithin, and the e2e residue named on the closed class node. The one infrastructure incident: padi's socket dropped ~00:50 and stalled four finished turns ~8h — the watch died loudly as designed; the human's \"Resume all\" resumed them","overnight-autonomy":"the human 2026-08-23 ~21:25, signing off for the night: ALL flakes resolved by morning; NO questions during the night — a stop-and-ask that would normally wait for the human gets the orchestrator's own best ruling, recorded on the lane with its reasoning, reported in the morning summary. The morning summary is owed: every lane's outcome, every merge, every judgment call made in the human's absence, and the flaky-tests Inbox node emptied or each survivor explained","ruled":"the human 2026-08-23 ~21:00 (chat): 'once #358 lands, autonomously work overnight to resolve all flaky tests with Grok. Preferably both Linux (localhost) and macOS (ci@petit) runs' — overnight autonomy granted for THESE lanes (supersedes the day root's approval gate for the campaign's own merges); Grok as author per the human's word","scope":"every open child of the Inbox's flaky-tests node at dispatch time: e2e-localhost-load-flakes (6 scenarios across 2 batches), serve-test-listen-flaky, pending-test-quiet-window-flaky (3 sightings, empty-ident cause hint — strongest lead), reaper-test-flaky, lock-test-flaky","standard":"the #347 treatment per flake: find what the test waits on and wait on THAT, not on time; test-race vs product-race decided per case, product fixed where it is the product; pin ≥ 20 consecutive runs green under load; CI preferably BOTH venues (localhost x86_64-linux under its flock + ci@petit aarch64-darwin under /tmp/olai-odu-petit.lock)","waves":"three authors at a time (the overnight precedent), lane-vpci counted in the cap: wave 1 (dispatched with vpci) = pending + serve; wave 2 (as wave-1 authors settle) = reaper + lock; wave 3 = the e2e-load class (6 scenarios, one lane). A fresh session resuming the night reads this prop and dispatches the next undone wave; briefs follow the briefs/flake-<name>.md pattern"}}
