{"id":"lane-cbtv-implement","parent":"lane-cbtv","ord":"a0","title":"implement on the linked PR + open PR + evidence","done":"2026-08-24T14:25:19-04:00","desc":"`pr` (as written, pre-typing): #365 https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/365 @ efc32b13 (+2256/−35) — reported 12:45 (1h35m): the adapter half extends the linked PR's approach to Monitor + background Bash (patch written upstreamable, pin patched, translation mechanical); the panel draws each background task as its own row (description, armed-since, elapsed via #324's rail), rows outlive the turn, events stream between turns, death carries the exit code; simplify pass unified isTaskOut (a real defect: the server's count forgot status). typecheck clean, unit 3560/0 + 77 browser, e2e 167/0 incl. a new scenario. Adapter verified against a real Claude session (Monitor, bg Bash exit 3, fg Bash, subagent). No deferrals. TWO RATIFICATION ITEMS held for the human: the shared 1 Hz clock now runs for hours under a persistent monitor (making it adaptive touches the commit pill too); offering the patch upstream to agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp (nothing touched there yet)","created":"2026-08-24T11:09:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T20:14:52-04:00","custom":{"fold-2":"RULED by the human 12:52 (after probing #365's design): a long-lived task's activity must not live only at its birth position — (1) while OUT, a fixed header strip (the #357 roster precedent) shows name + running-for, visible regardless of scroll; (2) on END the strip clears AND a fresh row lands at the transcript's bottom at that moment; (3) the original tool row stays as the arming's historical record. Sent to the author 12:52; evidence to be re-taken for the new faces; the human re-tests manually after the re-report + re-verification","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/365","terminal":"7dbc321d","upstream-issue":"https://github.com/agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp/issues/1038 opened 13:30 per the human's narrow ratification — extension