{"id":"incident-vault-restart-2026-08-25","parent":"day-2026-08-25","ord":"aF","title":"INCIDENT: the post-#395 restart took the vault down — recovered, four bugs filed","done":"2026-08-25T15:03:25-04:00","desc":"The chain, in order: (1) after the #395 merge + rebase, the running server missed the rebase's file replacement — reads served the stale set errorlessly, all MCP writes refused; (2) the human's restart then hit cold boot's all-or-nothing: two long-dangling `see` edges in features.olai (md-live-preview-editor, capture-files — removed days ago, tolerated silently since) meant NOTHING served, chat included; the human had to `mv docs/* docs.stash/` to get a working app; (3) restore surfaced a duplicate-id collision — the migration's restored `agent-opencode` roster row vs opencode's old row still in Trash (the fence counts trash; the trash copy was permanently removed, its desc folded into the roster row); (4) `orchestrator/lanes.olai` VANISHED in the stash/restore dance (cause unrecovered) — rebuilt losslessly from /tmp/lanes.olai.bak + the deterministic migration script (355 nodes changed, same numbers as the first run).\n\nThe live-board migration itself (this incident's trigger, not its cause): pr→pr-url as full URLs, merged split into date + merge-commit URL (dates recovered from the actual commits), agent/reviewer/repo/merge to ref ids, 131 `item` props dropped, every original prose value kept in its node's note (\"as written, pre-typing\").\n\nFour bugs filed on bugs.olai (see edges). The migration-fix commits: 1c30daf5 (spec amendments), 24f80b2d (the three vocabulary rows).","see":["cold-boot-all-or-nothing","stale-set-reads-clean-writes-refuse","broken-file-blocks-healthy-writes","last-good-banner-flood"],"created":"2026-08-25T15:03:25-04:00"}
