{"id":"overnight-2026-08-25","parent":"day-2026-08-25","ord":"aS","title":"OVERNIGHT ORDERS (the human, ~22:05, question tool)","desc":"The human sleeps; the orchestrator works autonomously. Ruled:\n1. **terminal-door / kolu#2216**: when td's reviews (grok+pi) fold and everything is green — run p0's SINGLE both-platforms /ci, **MERGE #2216** (the consumer-compiles proof is the gate), re-pin td to the containing kolu master rev, run td's own CI — then **HOLD td for the human's morning merge** (its manual mark stands). **EXECUTED: #2216 merged 35732510; #405 green 11/11 at 9170398f, HOLDING.**\n2. **Night queue: vintage-reads ONLY** — **EXECUTED: #406 merged e01a8763.** olai-subscribes untouched per the order.\n3. **Blocks: best judgment, documented** — used for: the keep-#2216-final guidance on pi's #405 MUST (the contract was honest, olai's usage wrong — fixed client-side, the tail-extent ask FILED as kolu-screen-tail instead of amended).\nNight tally: #404 (6530cf83), kolu#2216 (35732510), #406 (e01a8763) merged; #405 at the morning gate with its open questions on td-close.\n**WATCH NOTE: the night watcher (bdacmleu0) mutes cb9dcd13 — the #405 author holding to its merge (10-minute nags on a boarded hold). UNMUTE AT MORNING: re-arm without that flag when the human wakes or #405 merges.**\nStanding: auto-merge default; the pi rule; Opus reviewers cap-exempt; authors live to their merge; the 08:23 soak cron (validate-flip, night 2).","created":"2026-08-25T22:08:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T23:49:04-04:00"}
